WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:00.496
SPEAKER: So we're
going to give you

00:00:00.496 --> 00:00:03.870
an example of how easy it is to
use the identity of our proxy

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.090
to take a typical
corporate enterprise app

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.824
and make it available
to your users.

00:00:07.824 --> 00:00:09.990
Now the specific app we're
going to use in this case

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.490
is as enterprise as it comes.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.260
It's Oracle E-business
Suite running

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.420
on Google Cloud Platform.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.220
And as a company,
we want our users

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.710
to access this application,
whether they're in the office,

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.240
or they're out on the road.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.910
So let's see how simple
that is to do with IAP.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.760
Neil is going to click
the button to turn on IAP.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.090
He's then going to tell us
what domain he wants to publish

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.890
that application for.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.980
And now users in that
domain, and only that domain,

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.000
can access the application.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.040
So let's test it out.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.920
He's going to flip
over to a browser tab.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.500
Now first thing is, there's
no VPN software installed

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.170
on this machine.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.669
We are just navigating
into the URL.

00:00:46.669 --> 00:00:48.960
Now first he's going to try
his personal Gmail account,

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.540
which has not been authorized
for this application.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.150
And sure enough, he's denied.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:57.390
Now he's going to try it with
his corporate account, which

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.370
has been authorized.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:04.050
And he gets the username,
he gets the password,

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:06.090
but now he will get
prompted to enter

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.050
his second key authentication.

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:09.346
So if you look on the sides--

00:01:09.346 --> 00:01:11.470
I think we're going to
project that up in a second.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:15.270
Well, OK, trust me.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.270
He pushed-- there it is.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:17.500
He pushed the security key.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.510
I think you know
what that works like.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.600
And now he's taken directly
into the application

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.990
without having to have another
additional log in step needed.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:29.030
Not only is this easier
for the developer,

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:30.287
it's easier for the admin.

00:01:30.287 --> 00:01:32.120
And Lord knows, it's
easier for the end user

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.880
rather than hassling with
a bunch of VPN software.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.620
And it's more secure
because we're not

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:38.810
trusting anybody who
just happens to come in

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.890
through a VPN tunnel.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.610
So that's IAP.

